1. NVIDIA/RULER — VENDORED SOURCE
================================================================================

Copyright (c) 2024, NVIDIA CORPORATION.  All rights reserved.
Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

    Source:  https://github.com/NVIDIA/RULER
    Commit:  c3f5e3b4f87f97e048793bb510a3a6b19a46bf3a
    Fetched: 2026-09-02
    Located at: attnbench/_vendor/ruler/

The original Apache 2.0 headers are preserved in each vendored file, and each
file carries a comment naming its upstream path and commit.

    attnbench/_vendor/ruler/scoring.py
        From scripts/eval/synthetic/constants.py. VERBATIM — no modification.

    attnbench/_vendor/ruler/niah.py
        From scripts/data/synthetic/niah.py. MODIFIED. The needle/haystack
        algorithm is unchanged. Restructured from a CLI script — which calls
        argparse.parse_args() at *import* time and reads its configuration
        from a module-level `args` Namespace and global RNG state — into
        plain functions taking explicit parameters and a local
        random.Random(seed). Two upstream options raise NotImplementedError
        rather than silently substituting: haystack_mode="essay" (needs NLTK
        and a separately downloaded essay corpus) and type_needle="words"
        (needs the `wonderwords` package).

    attnbench/_vendor/ruler/variable_tracking.py
        From scripts/data/synthetic/variable_tracking.py. MODIFIED, for the
        same import-time reasons. The few-shot/in-context-example machinery
        (`add_fewshot`) is dropped as an orthogonal CLI convenience.

    Not implemented from upstream: common_words_extraction (needs
    `wonderwords`) and qa (needs a separately downloaded QA dataset).

    Consequence for comparability, stated because it is a methodological
    difference and not a footnote: this harness uses RULER's task-construction
    algorithm with a dependency-free filler-text haystack in place of real
    prose, and numeric/UUID needles rather than word needles. Filler text is
    a measurably easier haystack to search, so absolute accuracy numbers from
    this repository are NOT comparable to published RULER results. Every
    result row records this in its `haystack_mode` column.

    Full detail: attnbench/_vendor/ruler/VENDORED.md

