2. PiotrNawrot/sparse-frontier — APPROACH ADOPTED, NO CODE COPIED
================================================================================

Copyright (c) Piotr Nawrot and contributors.
Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

    Source: https://github.com/PiotrNawrot/sparse-frontier

No source from this project is present in this repository. One approach was
adopted independently and is credited at the point of use:

    attnbench/accuracy/sizing.py
        The prompt-sizing method — binary-search the amount of filler so the
        *rendered* prompt (template, needles, question and all, not just the
        haystack) lands at or just under the token budget — follows RULER's
        own approach and sparse-frontier's `sparse_frontier/tasks/ruler/`.
        Independently written; credited in the module docstring.

    docs/limitations.md records where this study's scoring is more permissive
    than sparse-frontier's, and states that numbers from the two are not
    comparable.

